.TH DASHBOARD-CTL 1 "2026-11-05" "pv-suite 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dashboard-ctl \- send commands to the dashboard control server (one-shot
/ batch)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dashboard-ctl
.RI [ options ] " [command ...]"

.SH DESCRIPTION
Sends one command (or a batch from stdin) to the dashboard's JSON-lines
control server over TCP or a unix socket, prints the replies, exits. The
one-shot sibling of \fBdashboard-cli\fR(1): no session, no completion
\(em the scriptable surface (the exit codes, one reply per command). With
a control token configured the wire is HMAC-signed: the client signs every
command and verifies every reply (the full sha256 of the frame, keyed by
the token).

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-control\-port
control server target: unix socket path or TCP port on 127.0.0.1,
auto\-detected (default: /tmp/dashboard\-8080.socket; env DASHBOARD_CTL
when unset) — same flag as the server itself
.TP
.B command
control command, e.g. inspect, show status, set battery on, request
reload, shutdown
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " N"
socket timeout in seconds (default 5.0)
.TP
.B \-\-control\-token
control auth token for TCP (env DASHBOARD_CONTROL_TOKEN)
.TP
.B \-\-control\-token\-file
the token from a file (the first line; must be owner\-only 0600); not
for use with \-\-control\-token (env DASHBOARD_CONTROL_TOKEN_FILE)
.TP
.B \-\-audit\-log
audit trail: a file path or \- for stdout; default: the XDG state home
.TP
.BI \-\-audit\-max\-mb " N"
rotate the audit log at this size, 0 = off (default: 10.0)
.TP
.BI \-\-audit\-files " N"
rotated audit backups to keep (default 3)
.TP
.B \-\-no\-audit\-log
disable the audit trail (default: off)


.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dashboard-cli (1),
.BR dashboard (1)
